    },
    {
      "type": "Text",
      "props": {
        "id": "Text-67c7f969-4b19-4a5c-bd45-93930e281bfd",
        "text": "<p>The movements in Odissi are built around the two basic postures (Mudra) of the Chowk and the Tribhanga. The chowk is a position imitating a square - a very masculine stance with the weight of the body equally balanced. The tribhanga is a very feminine stance where the body is deflected at the neck, torso and the knees.</p>",
        "style": "body",
        "align": "start",
        "measure": "normal",
        "layout": {
          "width": "text",
          "space": "s",
          "show": "all",
          "motion": "none"
        }
      }
    },
